From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] shell: Alt+Tab must walk the activities the shell tracks

Alt+Tab raised ValueError on every press and switched nothing:

  File "jarabe/model/shell.py", line 581, in get_next_activity
    i = activities.index(current)
  ValueError: list.index(x): x not in list

get_next_activity()/get_previous_activity() walk
_get_activities_with_window(), which keeps only entries that registered a
Gtk window with the shell. That was true in GTK3, where each Activity had
an X window the shell saw. In the modern Space an Activity is a Wayland
client inside the Casilda compositor and never registers one, so with two
Activities running the shell model holds

  all=[None, 'tv.alterna.Clock', 'org.sugarlabs.StopwatchActivity']
  with_window=[None]
  active='org.sugarlabs.StopwatchActivity'

- every real Activity is tracked, none is window-backed, and the active
one is never in the list being indexed. The emptiness check sat after the
index() call, so it could never run either.

Walk the activities the shell actually tracks, which is the same set the
Frame shows, and skip the shell's own window-backed entry: it has no
bundle id and is not somewhere Alt+Tab should land.

--- a/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
@@ -561,26 +561,47 @@
                 ret.append(i)
         return ret
 
+    def _get_tabbing_activities(self):
+        """The activities Alt+Tab can walk.
+
+        _get_activities_with_window() only sees entries that registered a
+        Gtk window with the shell. In the modern Space an Activity is a
+        Wayland client inside the compositor and never registers one, so
+        that list holds nothing but the shell's own window - which is not
+        an Activity and has no bundle id. Walk the activities the shell
+        tracks through their D-Bus service instead; that is the same set
+        the Frame shows.
+        """
+        return [activity for activity in self._activities
+                if activity.get_bundle_id() is not None]
+
     def get_previous_activity(self, current=None):
         if not current:
             current = self._active_activity
 
-        activities = self._get_activities_with_window()
-        i = activities.index(current)
-        if len(activities) == 0:
+        activities = self._get_tabbing_activities()
+        if not activities:
             return None
+        if current not in activities:
+            # The active entry can be the shell's own window, which Alt+Tab
+            # should not land on. Indexing it raised ValueError and the
+            # emptiness check below it could never run.
+            return activities[-1]
+        i = activities.index(current)
         if i - 1 >= 0:
             return activities[i - 1]
-        return activities[len(activities) - 1]
+        return activities[-1]
 
     def get_next_activity(self, current=None):
         if not current:
             current = self._active_activity
 
-        activities = self._get_activities_with_window()
-        i = activities.index(current)
-        if len(activities) == 0:
+        activities = self._get_tabbing_activities()
+        if not activities:
             return None
+        if current not in activities:
+            return activities[0]
+        i = activities.index(current)
         if i + 1 < len(activities):
             return activities[i + 1]
         return activities[0]
